  "relevance_note": "Narrative review of paediatric Behçet's disease whose only individual-level description of an HA20 person is one previously published patient: 'a patient treated for longstanding intestinal BD-like symptoms was later diagnosed with A20 haploinsufficiency [91]'.",
  "method_note": "Read the whole Markdown by hand; no script transcribed any table (the script only assembled the JSON). The paper is a review with no supplementary material section and no first-hand patients. All other HA20/TNFAIP3 mentions are group-level and get no rows: the 16-patient study [41], the 11-case Papadopoulou cohort [33] (HA20 named only among its final diagnoses), Zhou et al.'s five families [13], and 'familial BD patients' [89]. Table 3's 'HA 20' column summarises the disease, not individuals. One person was extracted under label rule 4 ('ref [91] patient'). No variant row was emitted because the paper ties no TNFAIP3 variant to this patient explicitly; it gives only the HA20 diagnosis. The title of reference [91] in the reference list says 'a Chinese Patient', but the review text does not say so; ethnicity was left 'not reported' rather than taken from a citation title. 'Intestinal BD-like symptoms' was recorded as an observed feature, but the checklist item 'gastrointestinal ulcers or inflammation' was left 'not reported' because the text does not say ulcers or inflammation. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is true because the patient is attributed to reference [91]. No contradictions found.",
